    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW255SXr86d2fAJcCNAASjKPb)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` after #503; independent of the other open PRs (one function and its doc line in `sp-bibprocess`).\n\n## What changed\n\n- Why it said \"date 2002 is a macro or a concatenation\": the date fixes only read values in braces or quotes, so `date = 2002` looked like a BibTeX macro.\n- A value that is only digits is now read like `{2002}`: `date = 2002` becomes `year = {2002}`.\n- Real macros (`date = mydate`) and concatenations are still reported and left.\n- Affects both `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-date` and `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-date-text`.\n- Doc line in `sp-academic.org` updated. `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 1 new test in `tests/sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el` (a bare number is converted, a macro is still reported).\n- Emacs 29.3 in batch: all 112 tests of `sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el` pass.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `C-; L b f d` on a `.bib` with `date = 2002` entries: they are listed as `year = {2002}`, no \"macro or a concatenation\" message\n- [ ] A real macro in `date` is still reported as left as it is\n- [ ] `A` writes them; running again finds nothing left\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDSLSq2vmaTSLDx6bL)_",
